.TH ZERODDS-MONITOR 1 "May 2026" "ZeroDDS 1.0.0-rc.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zerodds-monitor \- live snapshot or Prometheus /metrics server for the ZeroDDS runtime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-monitor snapshot
[\fB\-d\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-duration\fR \fIDUR\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR \fIFORMAT\fR]
.PP
.B zerodds-monitor serve
[\fB\-d\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR]
[\fB\-a\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-\-duration\fR \fIDUR\fR]
.PP
.B zerodds-monitor names
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-monitor
starts a DCPS runtime and exposes the process-global metric registry
either as a one-shot snapshot or via HTTP for Prometheus scraping.
.PP
.B snapshot
collects metrics for
.B \-\-duration
(default 5s) then prints the registry contents in
.I text
or
.I prometheus
format.
.PP
.B serve
runs the registry as a
.B /metrics
HTTP endpoint on
.B \-\-addr
(default 127.0.0.1:9991) until SIGINT or
.B \-\-duration
elapses.
.PP
.B names
prints the canonical list of known ZeroDDS metric names.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-domain " " \fIID\fR
DDS Domain ID. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-\-duration " " \fIDUR\fR
Run duration: \fI5\fR, \fI30s\fR, \fI2m\fR, \fI1h\fR.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format for
.B snapshot
:
.I text
(default) or
.I prometheus.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-addr " " \fIADDR\fR
Listen address for
.B serve.
Default 127.0.0.1:9991.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
CLI parse error.
.TP
.B 3
DDS or I/O error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-bench (1),
.BR zerodds-spy (1),
.BR zerodds-snitch (1)
